      {
        "linha": 523,
        "tokens": [
          "72450"
        ],
        "trecho": "REM-GNN   & \\num{72450}  & \\SI{0.28}{\\mega\\byte} & MLP & Feed-forward \\\\"
      },
      {
        "linha": 524,
        "tokens": [
          "301826"
        ],
        "trecho": "RadioGAT  & \\num{301826} & \\SI{1.15}{\\mega\\byte} & Attention & Multi-head att. \\\\"
      },
      {
        "linha": 525,
        "tokens": [
          "72194"
        ],
        "trecho": "RME-GAN   & \\num{72194}  & \\SI{0.28}{\\mega\\byte} & GAN & Adversarial \\\\"
      },
      {
        "linha": 546,
        "tokens": [
          "1812515"
        ],
        "trecho": "The capacity-matched control answers the complementary question. Trained on the same cells with five seeds, the multilayer perceptron with \\num{1812515} parameters and no message passing yields a paired difference, GNN-RF minus MLP, of $+$0.011\\,dB (95\\% CI [$-$0.126, $+$0.148], $n{=}8$, $p{=}0.86$), and equivalence within $\\pm$0.1\\,dB is not established either (TOST $p{=}0.083$); GNN-RF is better in four cells and worse in four. The trained model uses its graph, but at this sample size a graph-free network of equal capacity is not distinguishable from it. In Bauru~Q1, the cell with the larges"
      },
      {
        "linha": 620,
        "tokens": [
          "1812515",
          "72k",
          "302k"
        ],
        "trecho": "GNN-RF trains \\num{1812515} parameters, above the 72k--302k of the learned baselines (Table~\\ref{tab:cost}), and each blocked run completes in 2181--4032~s with peak VRAM of 7430--7512~MB on a single 16~GB consumer GPU, because neighbor sampling bounds the cost of each batch by its fan-out rather than by the size of the graph."
      },
