      },
      {
        "linha": 677,
        "tokens": [
          "1812515"
        ],
        "trecho": "A complementary methodological finding is that, on this reference, terrain features and distance carry the accuracy the learned models share. Damaging the graph degrades the trained model, by up to 1.72\\,dB when all edges are removed, yet a graph-free network with the same \\num{1812515} parameters is not distinguishable from GNN-RF over eight cells, and the learned baselines reach parity with it on a common cell. Training each quadrant from scratch shows no systematic advantage for the transfer chain. The uncertainty evaluation is a negative result: under spatial blocking, neither MC Dropout n"
